Detected semantic violation:

1. **Affected HTML snippet:**  
   [START]
   `<head><style>
		.offScreenLink {
			position: absolute;
			left: -9999px;
			top: -9999px;
		}
	</style>
	</head>`
   [END]  
   **Violation name:** `page-title-not-descriptive`  

   **Why:** The page has no `<title>` element, so the browser tab/bookmark cannot convey the page’s purpose or content.

I detected the following semantic accessibility violations:

1. **Page title is not descriptive**
   - **Affected HTML:**  
     `[START]<title>Failed Example 2</title>[END]`
   - **Violation name:** `page-title-not-descriptive`

2. **Missing landmark structure for the page content**
   - **Affected HTML:**  
     `[START]<body>
	<style>
		section {
			height: 100px;
			width: 400px;
			overflow-y: auto;
